# Portuguese 404.
#
# The docroot .htaccess sets `ErrorDocument 404 /404.html`, which is the English
# page — so every miss under /pt/ answered in English, including a dead link
# followed from a Portuguese page. `/pt/404/` has been built since milestone D
# and production had no way to reach it.
#
# ErrorDocument is per-directory in .htaccess context, so this scopes the
# Portuguese build to the Portuguese tree and leaves the rest of the site on the
# root rule. Deliberately a second file rather than an `<If>` block in the root
# one: this host is uploaded by hand, and a directive Apache rejects makes the
# whole file fatal for everything below it. The blast radius belongs inside /pt/.
#
# ⛔ Nothing else goes in here. A mod_rewrite directive in this file would stop
# the docroot's rewrite rules from applying to this directory.
#
# ⚠️ Points at the file, not at `/pt/404/`: the directory form leans on mod_dir
# resolving an internal subrequest, and the file is what the build emits.
ErrorDocument 404 /pt/404/index.html
